lc engages in the design, development, manufacture, and market of seating systems and components for passenger cars, commercial vehicles, and light trucks. It offers automotive seating solutions such as, complete seating systems, mechanisms, frames, foams, head restraints, armrests, and trim covers. The company serves automotive original equipment manufacturers in North America and South America; Europe, Middle East, and Africa; and Asia. Adient plc was incorporated in 2016 and is based in Dublin, Ireland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jerome J. Dorlack | President, CEO & Director | Age 44 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 65K people. Revenue per employee of $233K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $3K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $523 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Adient plc is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $1.1B market cap on $15.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -0% over the past three years \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 6% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $222M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 8.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 57/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 79% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 53% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 8% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (ADNT) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/52/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_ADNT_Volatility_111826083001_1795051801.html","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795051801.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Adient (NYSE:ADNT) Reaches New 52-Week Low \u2013 Here\u2019s Why","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/17/adient-nyseadnt-reaches-new-52-week-low-heres-why.html","date":"2026-11-17","timestamp":1794931737.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Adient (ADNT) Undervalued Following Earnings And A Bigger Buyback?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/automobiles/nyse-adnt/adient/news/is-adient-adnt-undervalued-following-earnings-and-a-bigger-b","date":"2026-11-15","timestamp":1794738245.647,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Understanding the Setup: (ADNT) and Scalable Risk","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/90/Understanding_the_Setup:_ADNT_and_Scalable_Risk_110826092401_1794191041.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794191041.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Research Analysts\u2019 Price Target Changes for November 6th (ABNB, ADNT, ALL, AMC, AMPL, APTV, BDX, BROS, CAVA, ET)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/research-analysts-price-target-changes-for-november-6th-abnb-adnt-all-amc-ampl-aptv-bdx-bros-cava-et.html","date":